WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.272 --> 00:00:07.976
&gt;&gt; :: I grew up in rural parts of Kenya, which have quite high rates of poverty.

00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:12.502
In our family, we used to get on our bicycles, each of us carrying

00:00:12.502 --> 00:00:18.428
three jugs, like three or four people, me, my uncles and my cousins.

00:00:18.428 --> 00:00:25.113
We would travel, like, 20 kilometers on a bicycle that day to go look for water.

00:00:25.113 --> 00:00:30.750
&gt;&gt; :: Four out of five people in the world don't have access to safe drinking water live in rural areas.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:37.944
This situation is particularly compounded in Africa where hand pumps and rural water supplies often fail.

00:00:37.944 --> 00:00:42.723
And one of the newest technologies that's now emerged in terms of mobile solutions and

00:00:42.723 --> 00:00:48.131
cloud-based computing is allowing us to advance with innovative ways to address this problem.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:56.402
The Reach program is aiming to make five million poor people water-secure in Africa and Asia.

00:00:56.402 --> 00:01:01.201
&gt;&gt; :: Groundwater is one of the safest supplies of water in rural regions of Kenya.

00:01:01.201 --> 00:01:04.444
So your being able to track the depth of the aquifers is critically

00:01:04.444 --> 00:01:08.764
important in being able to understand how healthy that water system is.

00:01:08.764 --> 00:01:11.707
We may be familiar with the idea of using one's smartphone or smart

00:01:11.707 --> 00:01:16.606
devices to carry around with us and to use to monitor our own health.

00:01:16.606 --> 00:01:22.044
And the idea here was: Can't we put some of those mobile health devices into the handle of a pump.

00:01:22.044 --> 00:01:24.741
&gt;&gt; :: So the data is really interesting.

00:01:24.741 --> 00:01:32.190
When you see the accelerometry parts, you kind of get these curves of the actual motion of someone pumping.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.975
When the pump is deeper, the weight of the water that you're lifting is much larger.

00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:39.449
So there will be more vibrations; whereas, when the pump is shallower,

00:01:39.449 --> 00:01:45.909
you're lifting less water, so there will be smaller vibrations.

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:49.790
&gt;&gt; :: Imagine you have multiple intelligent nodes that are all transmitting data.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:55.767
You have to integrate data in a cloud-based system from data nodes across an entire region.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:59.099
Tens of thousands of pumps in our case that needs to be done in a cloud-based

00:01:59.099 --> 00:02:02.811
situation where one has a huge amount of computing resource to be able to

00:02:02.811 --> 00:02:06.664
perform the heavyweight machine learning algorithms on the integrated data.

00:02:06.664 --> 00:02:12.668
We like the inclusion of the Azure machine learning framework which allowed us to port our

00:02:12.668 --> 00:02:19.706
existing R and Python-based machine learning tools directly into a safe cloud-based system.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:24.492
&gt;&gt; :: Azure ML makes fitting machine learning models much faster as I can explore

00:02:24.492 --> 00:02:27.994
the parameters base much quicker on the cloud than just on my own computer.

00:02:27.994 --> 00:02:36.624
&gt;&gt; :: I think making data usable and effective to decision makers is absolutely critical.

00:02:36.624 --> 00:02:41.792
Policymakers and decision makers have the responsibility to take very difficult and onerous decisions.

00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:46.402
And there's a huge information deficit in terms of how they should proceed.

00:02:46.402 --> 00:02:51.869
So the ability to collect data at scale in a way that's

00:02:51.869 --> 00:02:56.948
usable and appropriate for them is extremely powerful.

00:02:56.948 --> 00:03:00.540
&gt;&gt; :: Initially, it's used to take more than 30 days to repair a hand pump.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.712
But now, because we have this information, when a hand pump breaks down, we

00:03:03.712 --> 00:03:08.242
can repair them within less than three days or sometimes even 48 hours.

00:03:08.242 --> 00:03:12.133
That enables the villages to have better access to water.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:18.639
My hope and aspiration is to see this system making my village and other

00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:26.068
villages back in Kenya water-secure and moving them out of poverty.

00:03:26.068 --> 00:03:32.460
[Music]

